    "asOf": "2026-10-14",
    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Eleni Kounalakis is the Lieutenant Governor of California, having served since 2019. She previously worked for 18 years as president of AKT Development, a real estate firm, and served as U.S. Ambassador to Hungary under President Obama.",
        "cites": [1],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Eleni Kounalakis is the Lieutenant Governor of California, having served since 2019.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "She previously worked for 18 years as president of AKT Development, a real estate firm, and served as U.S. Ambassador to Hungary under President Obama.",
            "cites": [1]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "She says she would expand affordable housing by pushing to expand the Low-Income Housing Tax Credit program and better aligning it with tax-exempt bonds. She supports protecting public pensions through responsible investment strategies and opposes blanket divestment mandates, saying pension decisions should be guided by fiduciary responsibility. She plans to strengthen state-run savings programs like CalSavers, ScholarShare 529 and CalABLE. She has also said she would consider public banks to help low-paid workers avoid bank fees. When asked about divesting from fossil fuels, she has said her approach would be to focus on clean investments.",
        "cites": [2, 3, 4, 5],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "She says she would expand affordable housing by pushing to expand the Low-Income Housing Tax Credit program and better aligning it with tax-exempt bonds.",
            "cites": [2]
          },
          {
            "text": "She supports protecting public pensions through responsible investment strategies and opposes blanket divestment mandates, saying pension decisions should be guided by fiduciary responsibility.",
            "cites": [3]
          },
          {
            "text": "She plans to strengthen state-run savings programs like CalSavers, ScholarShare 529 and CalABLE.",
            "cites": [3]
          },
          {
            "text": "She has also said she would consider public banks to help low-paid workers avoid bank fees.",
            "cites": [4]
          },
          {
            "text": "When asked about divesting from fossil fuels, she has said her approach would be to focus on clean investments.",
            "cites": [5]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Her campaign says that as a UC regent and CSU trustee, she approved the construction of over 60,000 beds on college campuses. She also regularly voted against proposed tuition increases. As a California lands commissioner, she advanced a state partnership with ports to build infrastructure for offshore wind and cosponsored legislation for a statewide offshore wind plan.",
        "cites": [6, 7, 8],
